-- title:
--   Branch ideals at a crossing meet in (varpi_A)
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$, an integer $M$ with $M\ge 5$ and $p\nmid M$, a characteristic-zero field $L$ that is a cyclotomic extension of $\mathbb{Q}$ for $\{p\}$, and a primitive $p$-th root of unity $\zeta\in L$. Let $K$ be an intermediate field of $L\subseteq \mathrm{LaurentSeries}\,L$ equal to [`ModularCurve.laurentBaseChange L (ModularCurve.x1FunctionField (M * p))`](def/ModularCurve_LaurentCoeff.html#L103), the $L$-subfield generated by the coefficientwise image of the $q$-expansion function field of $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ over $\mathbb{Q}$. Let $A$ be a discrete valuation domain with fraction field $L$ such that $p$ lies in the maximal ideal of $A$ and $\zeta$ is in the image of $A$, with an $A$-algebra structure on $K$ compatible with $A\to L\to K$, and let $j\in K$, $j\neq 0$, have image the coefficientwise embedding of [`ModularCurve.jq`](def/ModularCurve_X0.html#L157). Write $X=$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChartModel A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L229), the pushout of the two affine charts $\mathrm{Spec}$ of the $A$-subalgebras of $K$ generated by $j$ and by $j^{-1}$, with structure morphism $f=$ [`ModularCurve.TwoChart.modelTo A K j`](def/ModularCurve_TwoChartModel.html#L252) to $\mathrm{Spec}\,A$. Let $k$ be an algebraically closed $A$-algebra field of characteristic $p$ and $X_k=X\times_{\mathrm{Spec}\,A}\mathrm{Spec}\,k$. Let $c_1:C_1\to\mathrm{Spec}\,k$ and $c_2:C_2\to\mathrm{Spec}\,k$ be proper, smooth of relative dimension $1$ and geometrically integral, with $C_1,C_2$ integral, and let $i_1,i_2$ be closed immersions into $X_k$ over $\mathrm{Spec}\,k$ (i.e. morphisms whose composite with the projection $X_k\to\mathrm{Spec}\,k$ is $c_1$, resp. $c_2$). Assume every point of $X_k$ lies in the image of $i_1$ or of $i_2$, that the fibre product $C_1\times_{X_k}C_2$ is reduced with exactly $n$ points for some $n>0$, and let $\varpi_A$ generate the maximal ideal of $A$. Let $\nu$ be a point of $C_1\times_{X_k}C_2$ and let $x\in X$ be its image under $C_1\times_{X_k}C_2\to C_1\to X_k\to X$. Given specialisations $h_1,h_2$ in $X$ of the images $\xi_1,\xi_2$ of the generic points of $C_1,C_2$ to $x$, the conclusion is that the two branch ideals of $\mathcal{O}_{X,x}$, namely the preimages under $\mathcal{O}_{X,x}\to\mathcal{O}_{X,\xi_i}$ of the maximal ideals of those stalks, satisfy $P_1\cap P_2=\varpi_A\,\mathcal{O}_{X,x}$, the right-hand side being the ideal generated by the germ at $x$ of the global section of $X$ obtained by pulling back $\varpi_A$ along $f$.
--
--   This is the local statement, at a crossing point of the geometric special fibre of the two-chart integral model of $X_1(Mp)$, that the special fibre is reduced there and is cut out by exactly the two branches: the intersection of the two branch ideals in the local ring is generated by a uniformiser of $A$. It feeds the construction of oriented étale crossing charts ($uv=\varpi_A$) for this model, used in the Deligne–Rapoport description of the fibre at $p$.
